   345	uncompromised (A8.3's sense of capture)" (:41-42). It names no set of receipts and no object for "signing
   346	capability". A8.3 (:72-76) bounds the tested property: under capture, "a captor cannot reattribute honest frames,
   347	alter honest signer sets, or carry honest signatures onto other bytes or keys". That property concerns honest
   348	service material, not only receipts issued before disclosure; the capture fixtures disclose the credentials before
   349	the honest signing processes run. A8.5 (:123-124) puts "preventing a captured or merged authority from issuing new
   350	attestations" out of scope. A captor holding both required channel credentials can sign and anchor a key assertion
   351	that names its own keys, without publishing it; receipts under those keys can then pass V1. Capture of only one
